<title>USA: Zinc stock tumble will strengthen price - Big River.</title>
<headline>Zinc stock tumble will strengthen price - Big River.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Zinc metal inventories will fall far enough by next year to prompt a strengthening in LME prices, zinc producer  Big River Zinc said.</p>
<p>Inventories were still too high to cause any price strengthening, Ed Schmidt, Big River's vice president of sales and marketing told delegates at the Institute of Scrap Recycling Industries meeting here.</p>
<p>He forecast an average LME zinc price of $1,150 per tonne or 52 cents per pound, some 15 percent higher than this year's prices.</p>
</text>
